/* book Worked example: Q: Design a balcony slab projecting 1.2 m clear from the face of a beam. Live load 3 kN/m², floor finish 1 kN/m², railing 1 kN/m at the free edge. M20, Fe415, 20 mm cover, 10 mm bars.
   1. Trial D = 140 mm, d = 140 − 20 − 5 = 115 mm. (With D = 130 mm the deflection check fails: l/d = 11.93 against 11.17.)
   2. Loads: self weight 3.50 + 1.0 + 3.0 = 7.50 kN/m², wu = 11.250 kN/m²; Pu = 1.5 × 1.0 = 1.5 kN/m.
   3. Mu = 11.250 × 1.2²/2 + 1.5 × 1.2 = 8.100 + 1.80 = 9.90 kN·m/m (hogging, at the face).
   4. Steel: 4.6 Mu/(fck b d²) = 0.1722; Ast = 250 mm²/m (minimum 168). 10 mm bars: 1000 × 78.54/250 = 314 mm, limited to 300 mm. Provide 10 mm @ 300 mm c/c at the top (262 mm²/m).
   5. Deflection: effective span 1.2 + 0.0575 = 1.2575 m, l/d = 10.93. fs = 0.58 × 415 × 250/262 = 230 N/mm², pt = 0.228 %, factor ≈ 1.77, allowed 7 × 1.77 = 12.41. Safe.
   6. Shear at d from the face: Vu = 11.250 × (1.2 − 0.115) + 1.5 = 13.71 kN/m, τv = 0.119 N/mm² < kτc = 1.30 × 0.342 = 0.445 N/mm². Safe.
   7. Anchorage: Ld = 10 × 0.87 × 415/(4 × 1.92) = 470 mm; run the top bars at least 470 mm beyond the face into the floor slab behind.
   8. Distribution steel: 168 mm²/m, 8 mm @ 290 mm c/c along the support, under the top bars.
   Answer: D = 140 mm; top bars 10 mm @ 300 mm c/c, Mu = 9.90 kN·m/m, anchored 470 mm behind the face; distribution 8 mm @ 290 mm. */
