/* book Worked example 2: Q: A one-way slab is continuous over five beams (four equal spans) at 3.5 m centres; beams are 230 mm wide. D = 130 mm, d = 105 mm, floor finish 1 kN/m², live load 3 kN/m², M20, Fe415. Find the design moments by IS 456 Table 12 and the steel.
   1. Clear span 3.27 m; 230 mm < 272 mm (1/12 of the clear span), so l = smaller of 3.27 + 0.105 and 3.5 = 3.375 m.
   2. Factored loads: wD = 1.5 × (3.25 + 1.0) = 6.375 kN/m; wL = 1.5 × 3.0 = 4.5 kN/m; l² = 11.391 m².
   3. Middle of end span: Mu = +(1/12 × 6.375 + 1/10 × 4.5) × 11.391 = +11.18 kN·m/m; Ast = 315 mm²/m; 10 mm @ 240 mm bottom (327 mm²/m).
   4. Support next to the end support: Mu = −(1/10 × 6.375 + 1/9 × 4.5) × 11.391 = −12.96 kN·m/m; Ast = 369 mm²/m; 10 mm @ 210 mm top (374 mm²/m).
   5. Middle of interior span: Mu = +(1/16 × 6.375 + 1/12 × 4.5) × 11.391 = +8.81 kN·m/m; Ast = 244 mm²/m; 10 mm @ 300 mm bottom (262 mm²/m).
   6. Other interior supports: Mu = −(1/12 × 6.375 + 1/9 × 4.5) × 11.391 = −11.75 kN·m/m; Ast = 332 mm²/m; 10 mm @ 230 mm top (341 mm²/m).
   7. Shear (Table 13), outer side of the support next to the end: Vu = (0.6 × 6.375 + 0.6 × 4.5) × 3.375 = 22.02 kN/m; τv = 0.210 N/mm² < 1.30 × 0.411 = 0.534 N/mm².
   8. Deflection, end span: l/d = 32.1; pt = 0.31 %, factor ≈ 1.53; allowed 26 × 1.53 = 39.7. Safe.
   Answer: Largest moment −12.96 kN·m/m at the first interior support (10 mm @ 210 top); end spans 10 mm @ 240 bottom; interior spans 10 mm @ 300 bottom; other supports 10 mm @ 230 top. */
