/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The riser R is the height of one step and the tread T its horizontal width; the going is the horizontal length of a flight (number of treads × T).
   - The waist of thickness t weighs 25t × √(R² + T²)/T kN per m² of plan, because the sloping slab is longer than its plan.
   - The flight is then a simply supported one-way slab on its horizontal effective span: Mu = wu l²/8, steel along the slope in the bottom of the waist, distribution bars across, and the usual shear and deflection checks.
*/
